# Switch the robot's operating mode by rebuilding the byobu session that
# implements it: AUTO tears down the mapping session and brings up
# config/sessions/start_nav.yaml (navigation), MANUAL does the reverse and brings
# up config/sessions/start_mapping.yaml (FAST-LIO2 + PGO mapping).
#
# Served by syncai_sys_manager on the relative name `switch_mode`, so it lands on
# <robot_id>/switch_mode. This restarts most of the stack — it is not a cheap
# call, and it takes as long as tearing down and re-sending ~40 byobu commands.
#
# mode values are defined as constants in RobotMode (MAINTENANCE/MANUAL/AUTO),
# reused rather than redeclared here so RobotState.mode and this request speak
# the same vocabulary.
#
# MAINTENANCE is REJECTED: there is no session spec for it. It is what get_mode
# reports when no session is running at all, not a mode you can switch into.
#
# Asking for the mode that is already live is a no-op that reports success —
# rebuilding would tear down a working stack (and, in MANUAL, lose an unsaved
# map, since pgo_node holds its keyframes in RAM).
uint8 mode
---
bool success
string message
